orceSkip, publisher trusts the caller and do not show the…"],["d6533874_f85f161b",35,0,0,"isn't this the state stored in webapp systems? If so, why this needs to be provided from client code...? Linked bug didn't help me to understand the details..."],["dae66c3f_c44eb50f",35,0,1,"Conceptually, instead of telling the condition of callers, could you make the API more likely instruction/request that publisher should respect? E.g. ``` enum class ConfirmationDialogAction { // ...…"],["ee36a798_f7128190",34,0,0,"if the state represents what is stored there, why do we need to re-remember the value...?"]],0,669],[7122849,20399,24,1.035,0.792,[[1,0.515,116,13],[24,0.242,29,6],[25,0.152,0,4],[26,0.061,10,1],[0,0.03,148,0]],[],0,670],[7072375,20402,1,0.174,0.115,[[10,3]],[],0,671],[7132723,20402,1,0.197,0.133,[[1,117]],[["74fec7cf_6ed5ceba",11,0,0,"will you do a test? 😊"]],0,672],[7198148,20417,47,1.77,1.388,[[0,0.837,149,40],[15,0.163,24,7]],[],0,673],[7209341,20423,206,5.298,4.261,[[3,0.898,20,189],[0,0.093,150,16],[26,0.009,11,1]],[["520d6767_c17664fa",36,-3,0,"Can this return nullptr? Maybe we can return the reference and avoid null-checks everywhere?"],["a2e3d0b2_6a88ecdc",37,-3,1,"Maybe let's keep these conditions for this RuntimeDataProvider instance somewhere. It's quite useful to know it by description, the code is not very straightforward AFAIR."],["b293b018_5b1f4f3a",38,-3,1,"What needs this?"],["d00e87d2_c37660e1",37,-3,0,"Do we always want to use it only through the client? Do you think it can be later owned by chrome_client which is a singleton, but not being a singleton itself?"]],0,674],[7213180,20425,133,5.576,4.507,[[0,0.945,151,1243],[27,0.026,10,33],[3,0.01,21,0],[4,0.005,103,3],[1,0.004,118,3],[26,0.003,12,2],[28,0.002,2,2],[7,0.001,2,1],[6,0.001,48,1],[5,0.001,22,1]],[["1af854cf_38737a43",39,-1,1,"Nit: Same comment repeated twice (a few lines above)."],["33c44a62_493de455",40,-1,1,"Nit: same"],["4334de56_1bafaeca",41,-1,1,"2025"],["5d4de485_563fcdfe",40,-